BT /F2 19 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 724 Tm (Understanding Homelessness ... Myths, Facts & Realities) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 696 Tm (Chico Campout for Compassion 2026  |  November 14, 2026) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 666 Tm (SEE THE PEOPLE. LEARN THE FACTS. START A CONVERSATION.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 647 Tm (You do not have to camp out to participate. Use this guide at home, in a classroom, or at a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 634 Tm (community gathering. Begin with a firsthand story. Then ask what evidence supports our) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 621 Tm (beliefs about homelessness.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 592 Tm (1. 'People choose to be homeless.') Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 573 Tm (Losing housing and refusing a particular shelter arrangement are not the same thing. Housing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 560 Tm (costs, available options, safety and family circumstances matter. Ask what workable housing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 547 Tm (alternatives really exist.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 518 Tm (2. 'Everyone without housing has an addiction.') Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 499 Tm (People experiencing homelessness have diverse histories. Substance use and mental health) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 486 Tm (conditions do not define everyone, and a person's appearance is not a diagnosis. Ask which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 473 Tm (reliable studies describe causes and pathways into homelessness.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 444 Tm (3. 'Refusing a shelter bed means refusing help.') Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 425 Tm (Shelters can have restrictions or conditions that do not work for everyone, including pets,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 412 Tm (curfews, family arrangements, access, and safety. Ask what other options someone can choose.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 383 Tm (4. 'Anyone with a job can afford housing.') Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 364 Tm (Employment and homelessness can overlap. Pay may not cover a local rental, and housing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 351 Tm (instability makes work routines difficult. Compare current Chico rents and wages before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 338 Tm (generalizing.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 309 Tm (5. 'Most people here came from somewhere else.') Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 290 Tm (This requires local data, not anecdotes. Check the Butte County Point-in-Time count and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 277 Tm (relevant methodology; explain survey limits before claiming what the numbers mean.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 248 Tm (6. 'Clearing an encampment ends homelessness.') Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 229 Tm (Moving a person or campsite changes visibility. It is not the same as obtaining a stable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 216 Tm (home. Ask how many people moved into permanent housing.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 187 Tm (7. 'Homelessness only means sleeping in tents.') Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 168 Tm (Families, seniors, youth, workers, and people temporarily staying with others can face) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 155 Tm (housing instability. Different programs count different populations. Explain definitions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 126 Tm (A 20-30 MINUTE DISCUSSION) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 107 Tm (SEE: Watch one vetted first-person interview or hear from a local guest. LEARN: Choose two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 94 Tm (assumptions and separate observation from evidence. DISCUSS: What surprised you, and what) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 81 Tm (local facts still need verification? REFLECT: What is one assumption you will reconsider?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 36 Tm (One Night. Many Locations. One Community.  |  Page 1 of 2) Tj ET
